1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:01,720
[Disclaimer:
All depicted events are fictional

2
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:03,460
and for entertainment purposes only;
viewer discretion is advised]

3
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:17,360
[Your Third Series]

4
00:00:18,350 --> 00:00:19,690
Do not disappear on me again.

5
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:21,080
And do not get yourself hurt.

6
00:00:22,310 --> 00:00:24,710
Get your act together soon.

7
00:00:29,180 --> 00:00:29,710
Take them away!

8
00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:30,710
- Don't hurt Jam!
- Let me go!

9
00:00:30,740 --> 00:00:31,560
- Stop!
- Jam!

10
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:32,470
Hey, be gentle!

11
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:33,880
The kid's this tiny!

12
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:34,880
- Hey!
- Hey!

13
00:00:39,310 --> 00:00:40,510
I was too lazy to go into town,

14
00:00:40,740 --> 00:00:42,320
so I asked some locals
if I could stay here for the night.

15
00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:49,980
Someday... you will find someone you love

16
00:00:52,670 --> 00:00:54,110
who loves you back.

17
00:01:32,789 --> 00:01:33,759
Mr. Sarm.

18
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:35,259
Here.

19
00:01:39,370 --> 00:01:40,890
What nonsense did you get yourself into?

20
00:01:41,090 --> 00:01:42,680
A weaver ant nest fell on me.

21
00:01:43,080 --> 00:01:45,850
I came across a mango tree,
and the mangoes looked tasty, so...

22
00:01:45,890 --> 00:01:47,000
I picked a few.

23
00:01:47,479 --> 00:01:48,000
Here.

24
00:01:48,410 --> 00:01:48,910
What do you think?

25
00:01:48,930 --> 00:01:50,990
But mango trees
are not usually free for the taking.

26
00:01:51,009 --> 00:01:52,090
I've looked around.

27
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:53,740
The tree's pretty isolated.

28
00:01:54,110 --> 00:01:55,220
No one should see me do it.

29
00:01:55,240 --> 00:01:56,150
You thief.

30
00:01:57,240 --> 00:01:59,630
You deserved to get bitten by
a swarm of weaver ants.

31
00:01:59,650 --> 00:02:00,630
Oh...

32
00:02:00,650 --> 00:02:01,570
Let's leave already.

33
00:02:01,670 --> 00:02:02,430
Come on.

34
00:02:02,460 --> 00:02:03,240
Take it slow.

35
00:02:04,350 --> 00:02:05,090
Ow...

36
00:02:06,090 --> 00:02:06,540
Here.

37
00:02:06,570 --> 00:02:07,650
Easy, please.

38
00:02:07,900 --> 00:02:08,830
It hurts.

39
00:02:09,610 --> 00:02:10,520
Hop on my back.

40
00:03:27,630 --> 00:03:28,110
Hm?

41
00:03:32,030 --> 00:03:32,600
Hmm?

42
00:03:35,190 --> 00:03:36,370
Hey!

43
00:03:47,020 --> 00:03:52,810
[Your Third Series]

44
00:04:03,110 --> 00:04:07,040
♫Still feeling lonely? Well, you've got me,♫

45
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:11,520
♫Keeping you busy every day♫

46
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:16,180
♫I might not be the one you wanted,♫

47
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:20,940
♫But give it time, you'll love me anyway♫

48
00:04:21,430 --> 00:04:25,970
♫It's your heart, so it's your choice,♫

49
00:04:26,010 --> 00:04:30,450
♫I won't ever stand in your way♫

50
00:04:30,580 --> 00:04:34,840
♫But when they make you blue,♫

51
00:04:34,880 --> 00:04:38,590
♫Can you please let me take care of you?♫

52
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:44,230
♫I'm here to love you as myself,
not as a surrogate♫

53
00:04:44,270 --> 00:04:48,020
♫Let me be your safe space
when you need a break♫

54
00:04:48,050 --> 00:04:53,040
♫Who cares if I'm not your first or second?♫

55
00:04:53,120 --> 00:04:57,800
♫At least being your third still counts♫

56
00:04:57,950 --> 00:05:02,540
♫I'm here to love you,
no matter who left you with heartache♫

57
00:05:02,590 --> 00:05:06,250
♫Just let me heal your heart,
lending you my aid♫

58
00:05:06,280 --> 00:05:11,390
♫Have faith and believe in love once more♫

59
00:05:11,420 --> 00:05:13,400
♫'Cause good love is your Lucky Third♫

60
00:05:13,430 --> 00:05:16,630
♫Your Third, can it be me, love?♫

61
00:05:16,670 --> 00:05:19,210
[Your Third Series]

62
00:05:43,490 --> 00:05:44,790
No need to sneak a peek.

63
00:05:45,590 --> 00:05:46,590
Come sit with me.

64
00:05:49,400 --> 00:05:50,650
Be careful when you walk.

65
00:05:51,790 --> 00:05:52,350
Right.

66
00:05:54,440 --> 00:05:55,190
Come.

67
00:06:04,030 --> 00:06:04,770
Go ahead and sit.

68
00:06:05,310 --> 00:06:06,360
Thank you.

69
00:06:16,640 --> 00:06:17,600
How are you feeling?

70
00:06:18,420 --> 00:06:19,330
Is your fever gone?

71
00:06:20,450 --> 00:06:21,420
It is, actually.

72
00:06:22,710 --> 00:06:23,670
Despite being this tiny,

73
00:06:24,750 --> 00:06:25,790
you're one tough cookie.

74
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:30,450
Do say no sometimes
when Sib gives you a task.

75
00:06:31,940 --> 00:06:33,150
I cannot do that.

76
00:06:33,909 --> 00:06:35,210
This is my job, after all.

77
00:06:40,100 --> 00:06:40,630
Right.

78
00:06:40,770 --> 00:06:42,200
How has working under Sib been?

79
00:06:42,630 --> 00:06:43,650
Hm? Has it been good?

80
00:06:44,100 --> 00:06:45,300
It has been fun.

81
00:06:45,790 --> 00:06:47,220
It is like playing a game.

82
00:06:47,960 --> 00:06:48,720
How?

83
00:06:49,070 --> 00:06:51,060
Well, I am given a task, correct?

84
00:06:51,100 --> 00:06:51,790
Uh-huh.

85
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:53,440
Upon completion, I will go...

86
00:06:53,460 --> 00:06:54,110
Yay!

87
00:06:54,130 --> 00:06:54,600
Hm?

88
00:06:54,750 --> 00:06:56,250
Mission complete.

89
00:06:56,750 --> 00:06:57,240
Gosh.

90
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:58,400
What a kid.

91
00:07:00,020 --> 00:07:01,720
And is this task

92
00:07:02,160 --> 00:07:04,190
the toughest of them all?

93
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:06,290
Mhm.

94
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:10,340
It seems like when I started this game,

95
00:07:10,790 --> 00:07:12,880
I may have chosen Hardcore difficulty.

96
00:07:15,700 --> 00:07:16,790
Do you want to give up, though?

97
00:07:19,090 --> 00:07:20,030
Not at all.

98
00:07:21,020 --> 00:07:22,790
I will just keep
being a burden to you like this.

99
00:07:22,790 --> 00:07:23,330
Hm?

100
00:07:24,430 --> 00:07:25,380
Snoop,

101
00:07:25,790 --> 00:07:26,790
did you ask if I wanted that?

102
00:07:28,790 --> 00:07:30,430
By the way, why the name "Jam"?

103
00:07:31,170 --> 00:07:32,430
Your mom a fan of Neko Jump?

104
00:07:34,790 --> 00:07:36,180
Otosan,

105
00:07:36,659 --> 00:07:37,770
my father...

106
00:07:37,790 --> 00:07:38,420
Right...

107
00:07:39,030 --> 00:07:41,890
He gave me a name that
sounds like my cousin's name, Nei.

108
00:07:42,320 --> 00:07:42,790
Oh.

109
00:07:43,590 --> 00:07:44,800
What about your name?

110
00:07:45,520 --> 00:07:46,380
It's dead simple.

111
00:07:47,080 --> 00:07:48,610
I have two siblings,

112
00:07:48,780 --> 00:07:50,060
and I'm the third child.

113
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:52,060
You do not consider Sib one of you?

114
00:07:53,790 --> 00:07:54,790
Of course, I do.

115
00:07:56,460 --> 00:07:58,450
But if we're talking about the same mother,

116
00:07:58,800 --> 00:08:00,120
there are only three of us.

117
00:08:01,230 --> 00:08:02,290
You already know that

118
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:03,800
my father

119
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:07,020
has had so many affairs.

120
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:09,060
I've lost count of how many there are.

121
00:08:14,440 --> 00:08:16,060
Sib walked his own path.

122
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:17,790
The same goes for Namnueng

123
00:08:19,100 --> 00:08:20,390
and Song.

124
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:24,040
Our parents went their own way, too.

125
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:29,000
That's why
I don't want to be with my family.

126
00:08:37,039 --> 00:08:40,280
So I chose to go far away
when I was heartbroken.

127
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:47,780
Even though I seem so cheerful,

128
00:08:50,190 --> 00:08:51,570
I do get lonely.

129
00:08:52,790 --> 00:08:54,100
It is okay.

130
00:08:54,510 --> 00:08:55,790
Once you get back home,

131
00:08:56,120 --> 00:08:57,590
I will create a Tinder account for you.

132
00:08:59,040 --> 00:09:00,190
Paint thinner is my forte.

133
00:09:01,630 --> 00:09:03,850
That is why you are always this high.

134
00:09:03,870 --> 00:09:04,340
Right.

135
00:09:04,990 --> 00:09:06,260
You're not wrong.

136
00:09:11,140 --> 00:09:12,060
Honestly,

137
00:09:14,980 --> 00:09:17,070
we've been through so much together.

138
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:20,550
How about we become friends?

139
00:09:25,220 --> 00:09:26,440
Would that be a good idea?

140
00:09:26,850 --> 00:09:28,300
I am way younger than you.

141
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:29,820
I cannot treat you like a friend, can I?

142
00:09:30,100 --> 00:09:31,750
Oh, how about this?

143
00:09:32,220 --> 00:09:35,040
Just ignore the fact that I'm almost 30

144
00:09:35,130 --> 00:09:37,050
and you're only 23.

145
00:09:38,260 --> 00:09:39,020
How does that sound?

146
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:41,650
Are you serious?

147
00:09:41,670 --> 00:09:42,350
Mm.

148
00:09:42,630 --> 00:09:43,970
Feel free to be yourself with me.

149
00:09:44,260 --> 00:09:44,860
Sure.

150
00:09:44,880 --> 00:09:45,350
Mm.

151
00:09:46,240 --> 00:09:47,830
Let me ask you something, then...

152
00:09:48,100 --> 00:09:48,770
What?

153
00:09:49,100 --> 00:09:51,350
Why the hell did you leave your job behind?

154
00:09:51,840 --> 00:09:52,350
Huh?

155
00:09:53,910 --> 00:09:55,190
Just kidding.

156
00:09:55,690 --> 00:09:56,570
That's a bit harsh.

157
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:01,820
It's starting to get cold lying here.

158
00:10:02,010 --> 00:10:02,540
Hm?

159
00:10:03,220 --> 00:10:04,350
Hug me, please?

160
00:10:05,700 --> 00:10:08,310
Well, you are lying there shirtless.

161
00:10:08,350 --> 00:10:09,630
So cold.

162
00:10:09,890 --> 00:10:10,840
Can I have a hug?

163
00:10:10,990 --> 00:10:12,590
Do you want to use this, then?

164
00:10:12,630 --> 00:10:14,060
I don't want it.

165
00:10:14,980 --> 00:10:15,630
A hug, please.

166
00:10:16,140 --> 00:10:16,860
Will you?

167
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:25,550
Please?

168
00:10:25,590 --> 00:10:26,970
It's so cold.

169
00:10:27,210 --> 00:10:28,380
Hurry up, please?

170
00:10:28,810 --> 00:10:29,790
I'm freezing.

171
00:10:32,420 --> 00:10:34,320
Just look at the way you dress.

172
00:10:39,830 --> 00:10:41,060
Just a bit more.

173
00:10:41,080 --> 00:10:42,210
A bit more, please?

174
00:10:42,940 --> 00:10:44,350
A little bit more, please?

175
00:10:47,820 --> 00:10:49,120
A bit more, please?

176
00:10:51,190 --> 00:10:52,500
Feeling warm now?

177
00:10:52,540 --> 00:10:53,410
Just a little bit more.

178
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,050
Are you shivering from the cold
or from being possessed?

179
00:11:15,550 --> 00:11:16,230
Okay.

180
00:11:16,260 --> 00:11:17,020
Right.

181
00:11:19,700 --> 00:11:20,760
I've decided.

182
00:11:21,100 --> 00:11:22,300
We're heading back to Ko Pha-ngan tomorrow.

183
00:11:23,510 --> 00:11:26,230
After getting your stuff from the bungalow,
will you return to Pak Chong?

184
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:27,660
As for the latter...

185
00:11:28,350 --> 00:11:30,230
let me think about it first.

186
00:11:32,980 --> 00:11:34,590
You do not miss your family?

187
00:11:38,230 --> 00:11:39,600
Well, I like the sea.

188
00:11:40,050 --> 00:11:41,230
I love the ocean,

189
00:11:41,790 --> 00:11:42,850
the fish,

190
00:11:43,320 --> 00:11:44,570
the coconut trees,

191
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:47,780
and the cat.

192
00:11:55,040 --> 00:11:57,560
But everyone at Adisuan Farm is missing you.

193
00:12:09,630 --> 00:12:10,620
Can I return there?

194
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:13,860
Well, why not?

195
00:12:14,350 --> 00:12:15,430
That is your home.

196
00:12:35,230 --> 00:12:37,230
There's a bull about to gobble me up.

197
00:12:38,620 --> 00:12:39,960
Then charge right back at it.

198
00:12:42,230 --> 00:12:43,230
Oh...

199
00:12:43,750 --> 00:12:44,610
No.

200
00:12:45,260 --> 00:12:46,880
You are a teeny-tiny tiger.

201
00:12:47,230 --> 00:12:48,620
You have no horns.

202
00:13:05,430 --> 00:13:06,980
It is okay, you see.

203
00:13:07,650 --> 00:13:09,600
If the bull really is waiting to
gobble you up,

204
00:13:10,230 --> 00:13:13,720
I will be the one waving a red cape at it.

205
00:13:25,330 --> 00:13:26,840
Are you scared of it?

206
00:13:32,620 --> 00:13:33,230
No.

207
00:13:37,830 --> 00:13:38,900
I'm simply disheartened.

208
00:13:49,010 --> 00:13:51,430
It is okay

209
00:13:51,440 --> 00:13:53,030
to let yourself be vulnerable sometimes.

210
00:13:56,100 --> 00:13:58,230
You do not need to act tough

211
00:13:58,550 --> 00:14:00,590
or carry everything
on your shoulders all the time.

212
00:14:03,990 --> 00:14:06,110
It is okay to cry.

213
00:14:10,070 --> 00:14:10,830
Nonsense.

214
00:14:12,760 --> 00:14:14,230
Tough guys like me

215
00:14:14,630 --> 00:14:15,630
don't cry.

216
00:14:16,930 --> 00:14:18,230
That is not true at all.

217
00:14:19,230 --> 00:14:22,470
Did you come up with that yourself,
or did someone else?

218
00:14:27,230 --> 00:14:29,010
You will always be who you are,

219
00:14:29,970 --> 00:14:31,750
a teeny-tiny tiger.

220
00:14:37,800 --> 00:14:38,990
It's just a "tiger."

221
00:14:49,840 --> 00:14:51,420
I guess it's time to go home.

222
00:14:51,890 --> 00:14:54,610
Handsome guys don't stay heartbroken for long.

223
00:14:56,440 --> 00:15:02,610
♫It seems like something's moving♫

224
00:15:02,630 --> 00:15:09,210
♫What's in my heart isn't too much, but I only♫

225
00:15:09,230 --> 00:15:13,380
♫I only wish you nothing but the best♫

226
00:15:13,400 --> 00:15:17,780
♫Hoping your smile will never fade♫

227
00:15:17,800 --> 00:15:22,500
♫That's all, for I don't wish
to take someone's place♫

228
00:15:22,520 --> 00:15:26,830
♫I'll simply be right here, always within reach♫

229
00:15:26,850 --> 00:15:31,390
♫Like a gentle breeze bringing you peace♫

230
00:15:31,410 --> 00:15:38,230
♫I'll stay right here by your side, always♫

231
00:15:44,750 --> 00:15:50,610
♫I'll stay right here by your side♫

232
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:19,680
You look stiff.

233
00:16:20,610 --> 00:16:22,150
Did you get Botox or something?

234
00:16:23,190 --> 00:16:23,830
I'm sorry,

235
00:16:26,390 --> 00:16:27,280
but are we friends or what?

236
00:16:28,420 --> 00:16:30,770
Last night, you said we should be friends.

237
00:16:31,200 --> 00:16:32,380
No offense, but listen.

238
00:16:33,790 --> 00:16:35,170
Just forget about last night.

239
00:16:39,660 --> 00:16:41,290
You mean when you cried?

240
00:16:42,130 --> 00:16:42,630
Ji.

241
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:44,480
Ra.

242
00:16:45,680 --> 00:16:46,270
Nat!

243
00:16:48,190 --> 00:16:49,700
What about it?

244
00:16:56,180 --> 00:16:57,030
- There.
- Ow!

245
00:16:57,430 --> 00:16:58,420
- Take that.
- Ouch!

246
00:16:58,760 --> 00:17:00,010
- There.
- Ow!

247
00:17:00,030 --> 00:17:00,570
- There!
- Ouch!

248
00:17:00,590 --> 00:17:01,010
- There!
- It hurts!

249
00:17:01,030 --> 00:17:02,010
- There, there, there.
- Ow, ow.

250
00:17:02,030 --> 00:17:04,010
I will hit you all over!

251
00:17:04,030 --> 00:17:05,319
- There!
- Why are you hitting me?

252
00:17:05,339 --> 00:17:07,030
I am exorcising whatever is possessing you.

253
00:17:07,670 --> 00:17:09,220
Have a taste of my palm.

254
00:17:09,240 --> 00:17:10,609
- There, there, there.
- Ouch, ouch, ouch.

255
00:17:10,630 --> 00:17:11,730
You got me.

256
00:17:11,750 --> 00:17:12,930
- Is the ghost gone?
- Stop!

257
00:17:12,950 --> 00:17:13,930
- You got me now.
- Is it gone?

258
00:17:13,950 --> 00:17:16,310
The ghost will lash out
if you hit me one more time.

259
00:17:20,770 --> 00:17:22,270
Well, you played along.

260
00:17:23,910 --> 00:17:25,190
In case you don't know,

261
00:17:25,760 --> 00:17:26,800
I am

262
00:17:26,819 --> 00:17:27,369
strict!

263
00:17:27,390 --> 00:17:28,170
Serious!

264
00:17:28,190 --> 00:17:28,950
Intimidating!

265
00:17:28,970 --> 00:17:30,000
And fearsome.

266
00:17:30,390 --> 00:17:31,920
You should be respectful and scared

267
00:17:32,150 --> 00:17:33,900
rather than treating me like a joke.

268
00:17:35,580 --> 00:17:36,350
Understood?

269
00:17:37,620 --> 00:17:38,800
I understand.

270
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:40,880
Gosh...

271
00:17:41,750 --> 00:17:43,570
I was laughing at you for trying to lash out.

272
00:17:44,720 --> 00:17:45,680
- Roar!
- Whoa!

273
00:17:46,050 --> 00:17:46,390
There.

274
00:17:46,540 --> 00:17:47,390
Hey!

275
00:17:48,390 --> 00:17:49,640
That actually scared me.

276
00:17:49,990 --> 00:17:50,950
Serves you right.

277
00:17:51,310 --> 00:17:52,160
Take that.

278
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:54,310
One more time.

279
00:17:56,930 --> 00:17:57,590
By the way...

280
00:17:59,580 --> 00:18:00,030
Hm?

281
00:18:01,720 --> 00:18:03,410
Once we make it to the island,

282
00:18:07,150 --> 00:18:08,250
what happens next...

283
00:18:08,270 --> 00:18:09,230
for us?

284
00:18:11,990 --> 00:18:12,600
Sorry?

285
00:18:14,620 --> 00:18:15,470
I mean...

286
00:18:15,990 --> 00:18:17,910
what will you do next?

287
00:18:18,780 --> 00:18:19,400
You.

288
00:18:24,460 --> 00:18:25,420
What about you?

289
00:18:25,830 --> 00:18:27,040
Will you return home?

290
00:18:28,280 --> 00:18:29,360
What if I chose not to?

291
00:18:32,960 --> 00:18:33,750
Mm...

292
00:18:36,730 --> 00:18:39,990
I would probably stay here
trying to convince you for a few more days.

293
00:18:41,590 --> 00:18:43,590
But eventually, I will have to go home.

294
00:18:44,470 --> 00:18:45,700
I miss my cat.

295
00:18:47,350 --> 00:18:47,830
Hm?

296
00:18:48,790 --> 00:18:49,450
You miss your cat?

297
00:18:49,470 --> 00:18:50,190
Mm.

298
00:18:51,300 --> 00:18:52,430
And do you miss me?

299
00:18:55,430 --> 00:18:57,600
And why do I have to miss you?

300
00:18:57,730 --> 00:18:58,150
Huh?

301
00:18:58,720 --> 00:18:59,780
Well, that's because

302
00:19:00,480 --> 00:19:01,900
I'm a teeny-tiny tiger, aren't I?

303
00:19:02,280 --> 00:19:03,600
That's basically a cat.

304
00:19:05,620 --> 00:19:07,150
Meow.

305
00:19:11,190 --> 00:19:13,220
Does a teeny-tiny tiger usually meow?

306
00:19:13,240 --> 00:19:13,790
Mm.

307
00:19:14,030 --> 00:19:15,460
Should it not be...

308
00:19:15,950 --> 00:19:17,190
"beep, beep"

309
00:19:17,800 --> 00:19:18,610
instead?

310
00:19:18,630 --> 00:19:19,390
Hm?

311
00:19:22,170 --> 00:19:22,940
What about you?

312
00:19:23,700 --> 00:19:24,810
Do you honk if I squeeze you

313
00:19:24,830 --> 00:19:25,380
like this?

314
00:19:25,600 --> 00:19:25,960
Hm?

315
00:19:25,980 --> 00:19:27,090
Beep, beep, beep.

316
00:19:27,110 --> 00:19:28,610
- Beep, beep, beep.
- What are you doing?

317
00:19:28,630 --> 00:19:29,630
Oh...

318
00:19:29,650 --> 00:19:31,440
What is with all the beeping?

319
00:19:31,980 --> 00:19:32,810
I guess I'll stop.

320
00:19:32,840 --> 00:19:34,280
I guess you are still possessed.

321
00:19:35,090 --> 00:19:35,690
Beep.

322
00:19:35,710 --> 00:19:36,380
Beep!

323
00:19:36,560 --> 00:19:37,440
Is it gone?

324
00:19:37,460 --> 00:19:38,300
Is it gone now?

325
00:19:39,400 --> 00:19:40,190
Beep!

326
00:19:40,380 --> 00:19:41,330
Mm.

327
00:19:41,440 --> 00:19:41,920
Beep!

328
00:19:41,980 --> 00:19:42,380
Beep!

329
00:19:42,630 --> 00:19:43,220
Beep!

330
00:19:49,050 --> 00:19:50,040
You and I

331
00:19:50,120 --> 00:19:51,840
always find a way to have a laugh, don't we?

332
00:19:54,320 --> 00:19:56,980
Do I also have to
accidentally trip and kiss you

333
00:19:57,350 --> 00:19:58,700
for the sake of realism?

334
00:20:05,740 --> 00:20:06,610
At this rate,

335
00:20:07,360 --> 00:20:08,470
a kiss is a no-brainer, isn't it?

336
00:20:24,070 --> 00:20:25,630
The boat's here!

337
00:20:27,270 --> 00:20:28,050
Hey!

338
00:20:28,070 --> 00:20:28,880
The boat is here.

339
00:20:29,040 --> 00:20:29,920
Let's go. Come on.

340
00:20:31,150 --> 00:20:31,630
Ow!

341
00:20:32,270 --> 00:20:33,010
Oh.

342
00:20:35,800 --> 00:20:36,940
Hop on my back.

343
00:20:38,220 --> 00:20:39,650
Let me put on my sandals first.

344
00:20:41,520 --> 00:20:43,270
I can hold them for you.

345
00:20:43,680 --> 00:20:44,600
Here. Hop on.

346
00:20:45,860 --> 00:20:46,490
Three, two, one.

347
00:20:46,510 --> 00:20:47,020
Now!

348
00:20:47,040 --> 00:20:47,600
Ow.

349
00:20:47,920 --> 00:20:48,510
Ow!

350
00:20:48,530 --> 00:20:49,620
Have you gained weight?

351
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:50,550
Hey!

352
00:21:00,610 --> 00:21:03,890
♫Time stood still when I met you♫

353
00:21:03,910 --> 00:21:07,370
♫The way you gazed at me too♫

354
00:21:07,390 --> 00:21:14,130
♫Couldn't understand what I felt, I had no clue♫

355
00:21:14,150 --> 00:21:20,330
♫It seems like something's moving♫

356
00:21:20,350 --> 00:21:27,390
♫What's in my heart isn't too much, but I only♫

357
00:21:35,780 --> 00:21:36,230
Hey.

358
00:21:36,460 --> 00:21:37,070
Hm?

359
00:21:43,160 --> 00:21:43,870
- Boo!
- Whoa!

360
00:21:44,450 --> 00:21:45,450
Why did you flinch?

361
00:21:47,780 --> 00:21:50,080
Why did you lunge at me, then?

362
00:21:50,080 --> 00:21:50,560
What?

363
00:21:51,320 --> 00:21:53,020
I was going to tell you that we're here.

364
00:21:53,430 --> 00:21:54,560
But you zoned out.

365
00:21:55,600 --> 00:21:56,280
That's why

366
00:21:56,790 --> 00:21:57,520
- I did this!
- Whoa!

367
00:21:57,640 --> 00:21:58,360
Like that.

368
00:21:58,710 --> 00:21:59,630
Hey.

369
00:22:00,030 --> 00:22:02,080
Haven't you been
complaining about your eyes hurting?

370
00:22:03,430 --> 00:22:04,380
So here we are.

371
00:22:04,680 --> 00:22:05,880
Well, yes.

372
00:22:07,310 --> 00:22:08,880
Him kissing me...

373
00:22:09,120 --> 00:22:10,780
was it just to tease me,

374
00:22:11,390 --> 00:22:13,490
or did it mean something else?

375
00:22:13,810 --> 00:22:15,230
I think I should go now.

376
00:22:16,620 --> 00:22:16,990
Fine.

377
00:22:17,320 --> 00:22:18,420
Want me to stay with you?

378
00:22:19,030 --> 00:22:20,210
That is okay.

379
00:22:20,620 --> 00:22:21,960
Go for a walk in the meantime.

380
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:22,850
Well, sure.

381
00:22:23,500 --> 00:22:25,570
Let's meet at the same spot.

382
00:22:25,590 --> 00:22:26,280
Here.

383
00:22:26,300 --> 00:22:26,870
Mm.

384
00:22:29,480 --> 00:22:30,390
Bam...

385
00:22:30,410 --> 00:22:31,850
This way.

386
00:22:32,680 --> 00:22:34,380
Ta-da...

387
00:22:41,320 --> 00:22:42,500
Woo-hoo!

388
00:22:42,520 --> 00:22:43,440
Bam, bam!

389
00:23:34,830 --> 00:23:36,050
Whoa...

390
00:23:40,960 --> 00:23:41,590
Oh.

391
00:23:42,150 --> 00:23:43,350
What a lovely pair of glasses.

392
00:23:43,500 --> 00:23:44,880
So sweet.

393
00:23:49,270 --> 00:23:50,040
Is that true?

394
00:23:51,950 --> 00:23:54,090
I usually wear black-framed glasses.

395
00:23:54,110 --> 00:23:55,850
I am not sure if this looks a bit weird.

396
00:23:55,870 --> 00:23:56,640
It's true, of course.

397
00:23:56,930 --> 00:23:58,110
Why would I lie?

398
00:23:58,550 --> 00:23:58,990
Hm?

399
00:23:59,420 --> 00:24:00,820
At any rate...

400
00:24:01,840 --> 00:24:03,150
thank you

401
00:24:03,900 --> 00:24:04,830
for bringing me here.

402
00:24:05,990 --> 00:24:07,240
Oh, and...

403
00:24:07,280 --> 00:24:08,480
Where should we go next?

404
00:24:08,640 --> 00:24:09,460
This way?

405
00:24:10,740 --> 00:24:11,380
Shall we?

406
00:24:13,080 --> 00:24:13,710
Hm?

407
00:24:14,130 --> 00:24:14,920
Which way?

408
00:24:15,800 --> 00:24:17,230
You should go back to your bungalow,

409
00:24:17,430 --> 00:24:18,930
and I will go back to my resort.

410
00:24:25,200 --> 00:24:26,030
What is wrong?

411
00:24:26,750 --> 00:24:27,600
Oh, Jam.

412
00:24:28,910 --> 00:24:30,600
Why must you say such heartless things?

413
00:24:32,700 --> 00:24:34,120
What seems to be the problem, Mr. Sarm?

414
00:24:34,140 --> 00:24:36,270
Tell me if you need my help.

415
00:24:38,960 --> 00:24:40,060
I'm scared to sleep alone.

416
00:24:40,100 --> 00:24:41,100
Mind sharing your bed with me?

417
00:24:42,150 --> 00:24:42,690
Uh...

418
00:24:42,710 --> 00:24:46,050
Well, I'm being hunted down by someone.

419
00:24:46,070 --> 00:24:48,240
And there's no honor among thieves, Jam.

420
00:24:48,260 --> 00:24:49,710
What if there's more than one of them?

421
00:24:49,840 --> 00:24:52,170
What if there are two,
three, four, five of them, Jam?

422
00:24:53,390 --> 00:24:55,000
What if they find me,

423
00:24:55,220 --> 00:24:56,510
and they kidnap me?

424
00:24:56,530 --> 00:24:58,140
Where would you even find me?

425
00:24:58,160 --> 00:24:59,710
Didn't you say I'm just a teeny-tiny tiger?

426
00:24:59,710 --> 00:25:00,820
I'm just a little guy.

427
00:25:00,840 --> 00:25:02,630
How am I supposed to fight
professional thieves?

428
00:25:06,160 --> 00:25:06,860
And...

429
00:25:07,510 --> 00:25:09,110
we've already slept next to each other.

430
00:25:11,130 --> 00:25:12,570
So please, let me share your bed, Jam.

431
00:25:18,140 --> 00:25:19,140
Uh...

432
00:25:24,460 --> 00:25:25,320
Okay.

433
00:25:25,680 --> 00:25:26,660
Okay.

434
00:25:27,230 --> 00:25:29,280
You can stay with me for now.

435
00:25:29,640 --> 00:25:30,600
For real, Jam?

436
00:25:31,070 --> 00:25:31,990
Mm.

437
00:25:32,270 --> 00:25:32,790
Yes.

438
00:25:33,150 --> 00:25:33,750
Yes!

439
00:25:34,990 --> 00:25:35,990
Bam, bam!

440
00:25:38,100 --> 00:25:39,910
Come on. Let's get back to your place.

441
00:25:39,950 --> 00:25:40,950
I'm so sleepy right now.

442
00:25:41,680 --> 00:25:42,290
Let us go.

443
00:25:47,320 --> 00:25:50,610
[Uncle Mai's Kitchen]

444
00:26:01,610 --> 00:26:02,100
Here.

445
00:26:13,330 --> 00:26:14,600
Sarm!

446
00:26:15,130 --> 00:26:16,390
Sarm!

447
00:26:18,190 --> 00:26:19,390
Sarm!

448
00:26:20,150 --> 00:26:21,740
Where have you been, Sarm?

449
00:26:21,780 --> 00:26:24,030
Don't you know that
I've been worried sick about you?

450
00:26:24,090 --> 00:26:26,480
I thought you got eaten by a shark.

451
00:26:26,800 --> 00:26:27,550
Mm...

452
00:26:28,720 --> 00:26:29,640
Calm down, Lantao.

453
00:26:30,680 --> 00:26:31,770
I'm fine.

454
00:26:31,960 --> 00:26:32,640
Not true.

455
00:26:32,680 --> 00:26:34,380
You've been gone for so long.

456
00:26:34,640 --> 00:26:35,490
Mm…

457
00:26:35,760 --> 00:26:37,150
Well, I'm back now.

458
00:26:37,190 --> 00:26:38,350
I'm not a ghost or anything.

459
00:26:38,480 --> 00:26:39,320
Gosh.

460
00:26:39,950 --> 00:26:41,190
Enough already, Lantao.

461
00:26:41,420 --> 00:26:42,320
I'm fine.

462
00:26:47,080 --> 00:26:48,080
Are you hangry?

463
00:26:50,480 --> 00:26:51,190
No.

464
00:26:51,590 --> 00:26:52,800
Yet your eyes say otherwise

465
00:26:52,840 --> 00:26:53,600
Mr. Sarm.

466
00:26:54,240 --> 00:26:54,690
Yes?

467
00:26:55,680 --> 00:26:59,090
Sarm and this Japanese guy
were at each other's throats before.

468
00:26:59,090 --> 00:27:01,640
So how come they're suddenly
acting so friendly today?

469
00:27:01,950 --> 00:27:04,850
It feels like
they've got some sort of chemistry.

470
00:27:05,200 --> 00:27:05,730
Gosh!

471
00:27:05,730 --> 00:27:06,630
I'm stressing out.

472
00:27:07,450 --> 00:27:08,360
Oh, Lantao.

473
00:27:08,360 --> 00:27:09,360
Get me some boiled crabs.

474
00:27:09,560 --> 00:27:10,470
Make it a special one.

475
00:27:10,470 --> 00:27:11,180
Ten kilos.

476
00:27:21,040 --> 00:27:21,600
Hey.

477
00:27:25,670 --> 00:27:26,440
There's nothing going on.

478
00:27:26,440 --> 00:27:27,040
I swear.

479
00:27:27,040 --> 00:27:28,920
You'll feel better once you have the crabs.

480
00:27:29,110 --> 00:27:30,130
Please, don't be mad.

481
00:27:30,330 --> 00:27:30,850
Aww.

482
00:27:30,850 --> 00:27:31,520
Aww...

483
00:27:31,520 --> 00:27:32,550
Nothing's really going on.

484
00:27:33,660 --> 00:27:34,480
Whoa.

485
00:27:34,770 --> 00:27:35,810
Please enjoy.

486
00:27:37,130 --> 00:27:39,270
This might be your last meal, Jam.

487
00:27:39,660 --> 00:27:41,810
When did I ever step on your toes?

488
00:27:41,930 --> 00:27:42,790
You didn't,

489
00:27:42,960 --> 00:27:46,270
but you're stealing my precious one from me.

490
00:27:46,350 --> 00:27:47,630
I won't let you.

491
00:27:49,770 --> 00:27:52,490
You came back this time
looking all scruffy, rough, and rugged,

492
00:27:52,490 --> 00:27:54,450
but somehow
you're still irresistibly handsome.

493
00:27:57,720 --> 00:27:59,620
You're just as cool as always, Sarm.

494
00:28:01,310 --> 00:28:02,550
Enough, Lantao.

495
00:28:02,980 --> 00:28:03,700
Your dad's not here?

496
00:28:04,120 --> 00:28:05,250
He's in Pak Chong right now.

497
00:28:06,430 --> 00:28:07,760
Why didn't you go with him, then?

498
00:28:07,940 --> 00:28:09,560
Right now, the weather's lovely there.

499
00:28:09,720 --> 00:28:10,460
I'm not going there,

500
00:28:10,720 --> 00:28:13,000
as I'm waiting for my heart to return.

501
00:28:13,360 --> 00:28:14,770
And now, my heart

502
00:28:15,030 --> 00:28:16,680
is right in front of me.

503
00:28:21,950 --> 00:28:22,470
Hey.

504
00:28:23,910 --> 00:28:24,400
Hey.

505
00:28:26,190 --> 00:28:27,140
The boy's hitting on me.

506
00:28:27,560 --> 00:28:29,080
Then you might as well make your move.

507
00:28:32,200 --> 00:28:33,000
I'm making a move,

508
00:28:34,020 --> 00:28:36,470
but I'm not sure if this boy knows it.

509
00:28:40,990 --> 00:28:42,600
You are asking the wrong person.

510
00:28:44,270 --> 00:28:46,840
Tonight, I will get you on a daily talk show

511
00:28:46,840 --> 00:28:49,160
so you can consult them about
your heart troubles.

512
00:28:49,160 --> 00:28:50,000
Gosh.

513
00:28:51,280 --> 00:28:52,230
Oh, you.

514
00:28:52,980 --> 00:28:53,890
Lantao.

515
00:28:53,900 --> 00:28:54,990
Are the boiled crabs ready?

516
00:28:55,210 --> 00:28:56,460
It's taking too long.

517
00:28:56,490 --> 00:28:57,840
We're starving to death.

518
00:28:58,170 --> 00:28:59,040
My gosh.

519
00:28:59,040 --> 00:29:00,590
You have to give us extra
for taking this long.

520
00:29:02,130 --> 00:29:04,090
Ten kilos won't do. How about 20?

521
00:29:04,090 --> 00:29:05,280
Give us your entire stock of crabs.

522
00:29:05,280 --> 00:29:07,010
If you're this slow,
I'm not coming here anymore.

523
00:29:07,610 --> 00:29:08,590
Is it ready yet?

524
00:29:33,350 --> 00:29:34,200
What are you doing?

525
00:29:35,200 --> 00:29:36,580
I am texting Mr. Sib.

526
00:29:38,990 --> 00:29:40,580
He knows now that

527
00:29:40,580 --> 00:29:42,590
you are being hunted down,

528
00:29:43,490 --> 00:29:46,200
so we've been hopping
from island to island to escape.

529
00:29:46,200 --> 00:29:46,790
Mm.

530
00:29:47,640 --> 00:29:48,600
What's next?

531
00:29:50,870 --> 00:29:52,610
He has called off this mission

532
00:29:53,810 --> 00:29:55,720
and told me
to return the day after tomorrow,

533
00:29:57,470 --> 00:29:59,560
even if I fail to bring you back.

534
00:30:03,090 --> 00:30:03,840
What about me?

535
00:30:12,950 --> 00:30:14,820
I want you to come with me.

536
00:30:32,240 --> 00:30:32,600
Here.

537
00:30:37,880 --> 00:30:38,600
Come here.

538
00:30:56,950 --> 00:30:57,890
Is your foot better now?

539
00:30:59,200 --> 00:30:59,930
It is.

540
00:31:05,590 --> 00:31:06,840
Mr. Sarm...

541
00:31:07,520 --> 00:31:08,440
This is too much.

542
00:31:09,090 --> 00:31:10,710
You do not have to do this.

543
00:31:14,070 --> 00:31:14,820
Don't take it off.

544
00:31:19,080 --> 00:31:20,200
Is it for me?

545
00:31:23,850 --> 00:31:24,400
Mm.

546
00:31:27,690 --> 00:31:28,980
For what occasion, exactly?

547
00:31:30,760 --> 00:31:32,200
It's for when...

548
00:31:32,820 --> 00:31:34,380
you miss the person who gave it to you.

549
00:31:40,170 --> 00:31:41,840
Why do you always tease me like this?

550
00:31:44,200 --> 00:31:45,200
Don't forget me.

551
00:31:47,830 --> 00:31:50,180
After dealing with everything here,
I'll be on my way to you.

552
00:31:51,860 --> 00:31:54,050
Also, don't taunt the bull with a red cape.

553
00:31:54,590 --> 00:31:55,530
It's dangerous.

554
00:31:57,560 --> 00:31:58,200
Understand?

555
00:32:02,820 --> 00:32:03,730
Mr. Sarm.

556
00:32:07,040 --> 00:32:07,390
Hm?

557
00:32:12,670 --> 00:32:14,910
Have you moved on from Mr. PiMai?

558
00:32:23,100 --> 00:32:24,230
You mean forgetting him?

559
00:32:34,360 --> 00:32:34,880
No.

560
00:32:39,350 --> 00:32:40,580
No matter what, I'll never forget him.

561
00:32:48,490 --> 00:32:49,560
Understood.

562
00:33:55,860 --> 00:33:58,960
For six months,
I struggled with chronic insomnia.

563
00:33:59,110 --> 00:34:00,440
My whole life was out of control.

564
00:34:01,310 --> 00:34:05,280
I don't even know
when I started sleeping soundly again.

565
00:34:05,640 --> 00:34:06,840
Maybe it's when

566
00:34:07,270 --> 00:34:08,330
you came into my life.

567
00:34:10,199 --> 00:34:10,610
Oh?!

568
00:34:12,840 --> 00:34:13,310
Hup.

569
00:34:14,719 --> 00:34:16,560
Mr. Sarm is no longer possessed, no?

570
00:34:17,060 --> 00:34:18,520
What kind of ghost possesses him now?

571
00:34:18,730 --> 00:34:19,460
You crazy guy!

572
00:34:19,719 --> 00:34:20,380
Mr. Sarm.

573
00:34:20,409 --> 00:34:21,150
Whoa.

574
00:34:21,179 --> 00:34:22,489
You've leveled up now?

575
00:34:22,520 --> 00:34:23,679
You dare insult me now?

576
00:34:24,350 --> 00:34:24,929
Hm?

577
00:34:34,420 --> 00:34:35,940
You're avoiding me.

578
00:34:37,440 --> 00:34:38,429
I am not.

579
00:34:38,840 --> 00:34:39,810
Oh?

580
00:34:40,090 --> 00:34:42,090
Still refusing to admit it?

581
00:34:49,139 --> 00:34:50,120
Tomorrow...

582
00:34:50,920 --> 00:34:52,370
I think I am going to head back.

583
00:34:54,889 --> 00:34:55,500
Okay.

584
00:34:56,190 --> 00:34:57,000
See you again soon.

585
00:35:00,470 --> 00:35:02,010
You and I...

586
00:35:03,320 --> 00:35:04,560
Will we get to see each other again?

587
00:35:06,850 --> 00:35:07,560
Of course.

588
00:35:08,150 --> 00:35:09,090
Who says we won't?

589
00:35:10,330 --> 00:35:11,480
You'll want to see me again, of course.

590
00:35:12,210 --> 00:35:13,970
And you'll miss me a lot, too,

591
00:35:14,720 --> 00:35:17,950
because there's only
one handsome guy in this world.

592
00:35:19,300 --> 00:35:20,910
There are two, actually.

593
00:35:21,360 --> 00:35:22,480
Is that guy as handsome as me?

594
00:35:23,720 --> 00:35:25,110
And is that guy as quirky as me?

595
00:35:25,700 --> 00:35:26,270
Hm?

596
00:35:27,840 --> 00:35:29,770
So you know you love to act weird,

597
00:35:30,070 --> 00:35:31,480
do you not?

598
00:35:34,150 --> 00:35:36,950
Song is really friendly with me,

599
00:35:37,480 --> 00:35:39,950
and he is very kind to me, too.

600
00:35:40,800 --> 00:35:41,990
"Song is this.

601
00:35:41,990 --> 00:35:43,240
Song is that."

602
00:35:43,330 --> 00:35:44,710
When will you start calling me by my name?

603
00:35:44,950 --> 00:35:47,240
Calling you "Mr. Sarm" is just fine.

604
00:35:47,270 --> 00:35:48,010
Fine?

605
00:35:48,350 --> 00:35:48,880
Who?

606
00:35:49,030 --> 00:35:49,480
Who?

607
00:35:49,720 --> 00:35:50,480
Who says it's fine?

608
00:35:50,790 --> 00:35:51,590
It's not.

609
00:35:52,070 --> 00:35:53,030
I don't like it.

610
00:35:53,290 --> 00:35:54,580
You keep calling me "Mr. Sarm."

611
00:35:54,820 --> 00:35:56,350
Do you know how distant

612
00:35:56,350 --> 00:35:57,480
it makes me feel,

613
00:35:57,890 --> 00:35:59,190
like my heart is bleeding?

614
00:36:02,900 --> 00:36:04,750
You are always over the top.

615
00:36:07,720 --> 00:36:09,150
Actually...

616
00:36:10,020 --> 00:36:12,280
